🏥 Medical Data History – SQL Project

📌 Project Overview

This project is a SQL-based medical data analysis project using a medical data history database.

The project contains 34 SQL queries designed to explore patient information, admissions, doctors, diagnoses, allergies, demographics, and basic health-related calculations.

The main database used in the queries is:

use project_medical_data_history;

🎯 Project Objectives

The objectives of this project are to:

Retrieve and filter patient information

Analyze patient demographics such as gender, city, province, and birth year

Work with patient allergies and missing values

Analyze hospital admissions and diagnoses

Connect patients with province and doctor information using JOIN

Identify repeated admissions for the same diagnosis

Calculate patient counts and grouped statistics

Use string functions to format patient names

Perform basic health calculations such as BMI-based obesity classification

Practice SQL aggregation, filtering, grouping, sorting, and set operations

🗂️ Database Tables Used

The SQL queries reference the following tables:

Table

Purpose

patients

Contains patient demographic and health-related information

admissions

Contains patient admission, discharge, attending doctor, and diagnosis information

doctors

Contains doctor information including name and specialty

province_names

Contains province IDs and full province names

