📊 Analysis Performed

Patient Analysis

Examples include:

Finding male patients

Finding patients without recorded allergies

Searching patients by first-name patterns

Filtering patients by weight and height

Finding the patient with the greatest height

Counting patients born in 2010

Finding unique cities and birth years

Identifying first names that occur only once

Admission Analysis

The project also analyzes:

Total number of admissions

Same-day admission and discharge records

Admissions for a specific patient

Patients repeatedly admitted for the same diagnosis

Number of admissions by day of the month

Patients with specific diagnoses

Doctor & Province Analysis

The project uses joins to:

Match patients with their province names

Match patients with attending doctors

Find patients with a particular diagnosis and doctor

Display patient and doctor records together using UNION ALL

Health Calculation

The project includes an obesity classification using:

BMI = weight (kg) / height (m)²

A patient is classified as obese when BMI is 30 or greater:

CASE
    WHEN (weight / POWER(height / 100.0, 2)) >= 30
    THEN 1
    ELSE 0
END AS isObese

🔍 Example SQL Query

Example: finding patients diagnosed with Dementia:

SELECT p.patient_id, p.first_name, p.last_name
FROM patients p
JOIN admissions a
    ON p.patient_id = a.patient_id
WHERE a.diagnosis = 'Dementia';

⚠️ Note on UPDATE Permission

One query attempts to replace missing allergy values with NKA:

UPDATE patients
SET allergies = 'NKA'
WHERE allergies IS NULL;

The project documentation records that this query was correct but could not be executed because the database user had UPDATE permission denied / read-only access.

